  "print": "bird",
  "_about": "TYRANNOSAURUS REX (sculpt overlay, 2026-11-05, after Hartman's skeletals of Sue and Stan): 12.2 m nose to tail, the hips 3.15 m up -- a horizontal backbone balanced over the hips, a deep chest and gastral belly with the pubic boot under it, a long tail held level and deep at its root (the caudofemoralis), a short thick S-neck; a 1.45 m skull deep and broad behind, narrowing to the snout, brow bosses over forward-set eyes, lipped jaws; tiny two-fingered arms; massive thighs, slim shanks, a long metatarsus to three forward toes (the ankle off the ground). Countershaded: dark olive back, tan flanks, cream belly, scaled all over. (2026-11-08, review.py: claws) The claws RE-ROOTED (review.py): each a sheath as wide as the claw where it leaves the toe, sunk in it, the join faired (horn `fair`: grown out of the skin in its paint), darker at the base fading to its own colour at the point -- no pale cut edge where it leaves the fur. (2026-11-08, review.py: hand claws) The HAND: each finger one smooth horn (faired into the hand, a rounded fingertip) instead of a field cone and a six-sided tube that came out as blocky shards on the coarse grid round the claws' roots; the claws come out of the fingertips, 0.72 of their girth, along their old hooks (no fillet). (2026-11-08, review.py: fingers) The FINGERS (review.py knuckle_fingers): slimmer, two knuckles swelling along each, the arm's scales on them, each running into its claw -- the claw's base nearly the fingertip's girth and round, a sheath the finger ends in (they read as smooth sausages with a thin claw poking out).",
  "sculpt": {
